cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it as below."
title: "surrey-biome-pipeline: a two-extent test of scale-free climate downscaling against polygon-scale water stress"
abstract: >-
  Code, method and applied output for a controlled test of whether
  high-resolution "scale-free" downscaled climate data predicts polygon-scale
  vegetation water stress better than the same variables degraded to a coarse
  regional-model grid. Run at two extents: Surrey's Green Infrastructure
  Network, 144 corridors digitised as 153 polygons, where the contrast was too
  small to test the question, and a 100 km Fraser Valley elevation transect,
  where the degraded model beat the scale-free one on the point estimate in all
  32 configurations tested while the paired interval spanned zero in 31 of
  them, a consistent direction rather than a resolved effect. Also contains
  CDEI, a Sentinel-2 and Landsat index of polygon water stress, mapped and
  ranked across Surrey's corridors and checked against independent radar and
  climate data, which do not corroborate the ranking as water stress.
type: software
